{"open_points":[{"subject":"M07 PublicationMark.marked_at","kind":"time_source_and_representation","text":"`marked_at: datetime`","question":"Which authority supplies `marked_at`, at what step of a mark operation is it read, how many times is it read, and is the stored datetime naive UTC, offset-aware UTC, local time or another representation?","options":["Read an injected clock once after the project lock is acquired and store naive UTC.","Read an injected clock once after the project lock is acquired and store offset-aware UTC.","Read the ambient system clock at an implementer-chosen point and store local time."],"default_guess":"Use an injected clock, read it exactly once after acquiring the project lock and immediately before creating the mark, and store naive UTC to match the product's other persisted datetime representation.","witness":{"initial":"A confirmed project has a placement without a publication mark; the mark call waits behind another holder of the project lock while the local time zone is Europe/Madrid.","events":["The calling flow submits a valid mark request with the Portal photo id.","The first implementation reads an injected UTC clock once after it acquires the lock and stores naive UTC.","The second implementation reads the ambient local clock before waiting for the lock and stores an offset-aware local datetime."],"outcomes":["The record contains the instant at which the mark is committed, represented as naive UTC.","The record contains an earlier instant represented with a local offset."],"observer":"A later scan or repeated mark that reads the record, and any test comparing `marked_at`."}},{"subject":"A3 replacement whose new content already has a placement","kind":"contradiction","text":"A replaced source is a new photo.

A file replaced with other content is a new photo and waits for the owner's delivery.

Delivering content that already has a placement answers the REPLAYED member of = models.PlacementStatus with the stored placement and the current `photo_id` of its mark, if any, whatever name the request carries","question":"When a file is replaced by different content that already has a placement in the same project, is it a new photo waiting for delivery, or is it the already placed photo and immediately replayed?","options":["Content identity takes precedence: the scan reports PLACED or PUBLISHED and delivery returns REPLAYED.","Replacement takes precedence: the path is READY and delivery creates a distinct new placement.","It is called a new photo relative to the replaced file, but operationally uses the existing content placement; the text must state this distinction."],"default_guess":"Treat identity as content-based: report PLACED or PUBLISHED and return REPLAYED, while clarifying that “new photo” means only that it is not the earlier content at that path.","witness":{"initial":"Project P has `b.jpg` with content B, and B already has a placement and publication mark. `a.jpg` previously contained different content A with its own placement and mark.","events":["Syncthing replaces `a.jpg` with bytes identical to content B.","The caller scans project P.","The caller asks to deliver `a.jpg` using B's source id."],"outcomes":["Under content identity and A3 rule 2, `a.jpg` is PUBLISHED and delivery returns REPLAYED with B's placement and photo id.","Under the unconditional replacement statements, `a.jpg` is a new photo that waits for delivery rather than being treated as B's existing placed photo."],"observer":"The calling flow choosing what to offer or publish."}},{"subject":"A3 INV-07 Required tests","kind":"incomplete_invariant_test","text":"INV-07: a replaced file whose new content has no placement is reported as a new photo with the READY member of = models.ScanStatus while the earlier image and mark stay (`test_a_replaced_file_is_a_new_photo_and_the_first_delivery_stays`), and a removed file keeps its delivery (`test_removing_a_file_keeps_its_delivery`).","question":"What Required tests item shows that replacing a file with content that already has a placement also leaves the replaced file's earlier placement, stored image and mark unchanged, as INV-07 requires without the test's new precondition?","options":["Add a case where the replacement content already has an unmarked placement.","Add cases where the replacement content already has both an unmarked placement and a marked placement.","Narrow INV-07 itself to replacements whose new content has no placement."],"default_guess":"Keep INV-07 universal and require marked and unmarked existing-placement replacement cases, asserting that every pre-existing placement, stored image and mark remains byte-for-byte unchanged.","witness":{"initial":"Content A and content B both have placements in one project, and A also has a mark. A source path currently contains A.","events":["The source path is replaced with content B.","A scan and delivery of that path run.","An implementation either preserves A's placement, image and mark or accidentally rewrites one of them while resolving B's existing placement."],"outcomes":["All earlier durable artifacts for A and B remain unchanged.","The scan and delivery still appear correct for B, but an earlier artifact for A is changed; the stated Required tests never exercise this history."],"observer":"The owner or a later replay that reads A's earlier placement or mark."}}]}
